Nethack 3.0 patchlevel 3
file: msdos.c

Please do not trap the Alt-key in that way!

Those of us having (inter)national keyboards
m-u-s-t use the Alt-key to obtain Ascii 35d, 91d, 92d, 93d,
123d, 124d, 125d, et cetera.

Our local quickfix consists of a switch(ch), with the
cases above just returning ch, and default returning
the scanmapped conversion.

Otherwise everything seems to work just fine. Thank you.

